# The scheduled jobs. Run by supercronic in the `jobs` container (deploy/compose.yml),
# from /app, with the same settings as the API. Check this file with:
#   docker compose run --rm --no-deps jobs supercronic -test /app/crontab
#
# The container's clock is UTC. Times below are UTC, with the India time beside
# each. Every job's output goes to `docker compose logs jobs`; the backup jobs
# also write their outcome to the audit log (Settings → Audit Log → System
# jobs), where somebody will see a failure.

# 21:00 UTC = 02:30 IST — the nightly database backup to R2, sealed, then old ones pruned
0 21 * * * npm run --silent backup

# 21:30 UTC = 03:00 IST — orphaned-file sweep and old-notice purge
30 21 * * * npm run --silent maintenance -- --apply

# 22:30 UTC on the 1st = 04:00 IST on the 2nd — the monthly restore drill: the newest
# backup is restored into a scratch database and every table's rows are checked
30 22 1 * * npm run --silent backup:drill -- --latest
